 * metadata segment in that row (dates, location, timezone, creator,
 * participants) shares the exact same wrapper markup, and several of them
 * are conditionally rendered, so positional indexing (the ticket's own
 * `div.flex.items-center:nth-of-type(4)`) is fragile and was the fragile
 * path this suite is meant to replace.
 *
 * Anchor on the ONE thing that IS stable without touching range-mfe: the
 * `lucide-users` class lucide-react itself stamps onto the icon's `<svg>`
 * (see `createLucideIcon` — every lucide icon gets `lucide` + `lucide-
 * <kebab-name>` merged into its className, independent of anything the
 * consuming component passes).
 *
 * That class alone is NOT unique on this page, though: three components
 * render a lucide `Users` icon inside `#range-main` — this MetaItem
 * (ExerciseOverviewRoute.tsx), the participants card in the stat-card row
 * directly below (ExerciseStatCardRow.tsx), and the persistent admin nav
 * (ExerciseShell.tsx). So we scope to `#range-main header` first: the
 * overview's metadata `<header>` closes before the stat-card row begins, and
 * ExerciseShell's nav is a `<nav>`, not a `<header>` — leaving exactly one
 * match. (`#range-main` is RangeLayout's main element, which also excludes
 * the platform-chrome Topbar; it is the same root the issue's own reported
 * DOM path starts from.)
 *
 * `.closest("div")` then walks up from the svg — past the icon's wrapping
 * `aria-hidden` span, which is not a div — to the MetaItem's own root div,
 * whose text is exactly the rendered value: the localized
 * "{count} participant(s)" string, or the "—" em-dash placeholder shown
 * while stats are loading/erroring (#2183's fix).
 *
 * `timeout` widens the retry window for callers that need to wait past the
 * em-dash placeholder to the resolved stats read (the lane's cold-boot-
 * tolerant idiom — see exercise-lifecycle.cy.ts's 30-45s windows on a
 * spec's first live call). It is applied to both the `cy.get` and the
 * `.closest` query so the whole chain shares one retry window — an
 * assertion chained off the returned subject takes its budget from the
 * LAST query, so passing it to `cy.get` alone would leave `.closest`
 * falling back to `defaultCommandTimeout`.
